IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aca-dates`
IMPORT `aca-amounts`

-- Accident Compensation Act 1985 (Vic) -- weekly payments and compensation for non-economic loss, for an injured worker
-- whose injury was before 1 July 2014 (s 4(1)(a)).
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker. Every exported question is one the worker would ask: "Which entitlement period am I in?",
-- "How much are my weekly payments this week?", "Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period?",
-- "Can my application to keep my weekly payments be approved?", "Does my age stop my weekly payments?", "Must my
-- superannuation be paid?", "How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss?". Where the Act leaves a judgment to the
-- Authority or self-insurer (an assessment of work capacity, a determination of whole person impairment, being satisfied),
-- the judgment is asked as a fact and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions: s 4(1); s 91E (deductible amount, first and second entitlement periods, pre-12 November 1997 claimant,
-- serious injury); s 93; s 93A(1)-(3); s 93B(1)-(3); s 93C(1), (2); s 93CD(1), (3), (4), (5); s 93CE(1), (2), (3);
-- s 93E; s 93F; ss 100B, 100D, 100E (the ceilings, through aca-amounts); s 98C(1A), (1), (2), (2A), (3), (3AA), (3AB),
-- (4), (11) with Schedule 2; s 265; s 313.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("ceases ... unless",
-- "must not approve ... unless", "is not entitled"), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given; each
-- NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. An amount answers JUST the amount, or NOTHING.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Accident
-- Compensation Act 1985, Version No. 237 (2 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Weekly payments (Part IV Division 2, ss 91E-93F)`

§§ `s 91E -- which kind of claim mine is`

-- s 91E: "pre-12 November 1997 claimant, in relation to a claim for compensation in the form of weekly payments given,
-- served or lodged before 12 November 1997 in respect of an injury arising before that date, means a worker who -- (a) as
-- at that date, was entitled to compensation in the form of weekly payments in accordance with section 93A or 93B (as in
-- force before ...); or (b) on or after that date, was determined under this Act to have been so entitled as at 12 November
-- 1997; or (c) but for the operation of section 96 (as in force before ...) would have been so entitled as at 12 November
-- 1997".
-- s 93A(2), (3): a claim "first made in respect of the injury to which the claim relates on or after 12 November 1997 and
-- before 5 April 2010" / "on or after 5 April 2010".
-- A claim made before 12 November 1997 by a worker who was not entitled as at that date fits none of the three: the
-- weekly payment sections give it no rate (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN `the day the claim was first made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `I was entitled to weekly payments as at 12 November 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Weekly payments claim`
`the kind of weekly payments claim made on` `the day the claim was first made` `for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `entitled at 12 November 1997` `I was entitled to weekly payments as at 12 November 1997` MEANS
    IF `the day the claim was first made` `is before` (`the calendar date` 12 11 1997)
    THEN IF (`the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 12 11 1997)) AND `I was entitled to weekly payments as at 12 November 1997`
         THEN JUST `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: a pre-1997 claim by a worker outside the definition has no rate in ss 93A-93C)
    ELSE IF `the day the claim was first made` `is before` (`the calendar date` 5 4 2010)
         THEN JUST `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010`
         ELSE JUST `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010`

@export Which kind of weekly payments claim is mine under the Accident Compensation Act 1985 (s 91E pre-12 November 1997 claimant; ss 93A-93C)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured (before 1 July 2014)
      `the day the claim was first made` IS A DATE @desc The day you first made your claim for weekly payments for this injury
      `I was entitled to weekly payments as at 12 November 1997` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as at 12 November 1997, you were entitled to weekly payments (or were later determined to have been, or would have been but for the old s 96)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Weekly payments claim`
`What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` MEANS
    `the kind of weekly payments claim made on` `the day the claim was first made` `for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `entitled at 12 November 1997` `I was entitled to weekly payments as at 12 November 1997`

§§ `s 91E -- which entitlement period I am in`

DECLARE `Entitlement period` IS ONE OF
    `the first entitlement period`
    `the second entitlement period`
    `after the second entitlement period`

-- s 91E: first entitlement period "(a) if the claim is made by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant and relates to an injury
-- arising before that date ... not exceeding 26 weeks ... (b) if the claim is made on or after 12 November 1997, ... not
-- exceeding 13 weeks"; second entitlement period "(a) [pre-12 November 1997 claimant] ... 78 weeks ... after the first
-- entitlement period; (b) if the claim is made on or after 12 November 1997 and received by the Authority or self-insurer
-- before 1 January 2005, ... 91 weeks ...; (c) if the claim is received ... on or after 1 January 2005, ... 117 weeks".
-- Weeks are counted in aggregate, "whether or not consecutive", as weeks for which a weekly payment "has been paid or is
-- payable ... for all or any part of that week" (s 91E "week").
-- READING (fork F1): for a pre-12 November 1997 claimant the first period counts weeks of incapacity after the worker
-- became entitled; the count of weeks of weekly payments is taken for it.
GIVEN `the number of this week` IS A NUMBER
      `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim`
      `the day the insurer received the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Entitlement period`
`the entitlement period of week` `the number of this week` `of` `the claim` `received on` `the day the insurer received the claim` MEANS
    IF `the number of this week` AT MOST `first`
    THEN `the first entitlement period`
    ELSE IF `the number of this week` AT MOST (`first` PLUS `second`)
         THEN `the second entitlement period`
         ELSE `after the second entitlement period`
    WHERE
        `first` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`
            WHEN `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` THEN 26
            OTHERWISE 13
        `second` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`
            WHEN `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` THEN 78
            OTHERWISE
                IF `the day the insurer received the claim` `is before` (`the calendar date` 1 1 2005)
                THEN 91
                ELSE 117

@export Which entitlement period am I in this week (s 91E: 13 or 26 weeks, then 78, 91 or 117 weeks)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim` @desc Your kind of claim: a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant, one first made from 12 November 1997 to before 5 April 2010, or one first made on or after 5 April 2010
      `the day the insurer received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority (WorkSafe) or the self-insurer received your claim for weekly payments
      `the number of this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting this week, how many weeks weekly payments have been paid or are payable to you for this injury, consecutive or not (a week counts if any payment is for any part of it)
GIVETH AN `Entitlement period`
`Which entitlement period am I in` MEANS
    `the entitlement period of week` `the number of this week` `of` `the claim` `received on` `the day the insurer received the claim`

§§ `s 93C(1) -- whether my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period`

-- s 93C(1): "Subject to section 93CD, a worker's entitlement to compensation in the form of weekly payments under this Part
-- ceases upon the expiry of the second entitlement period unless -- (a) subject to paragraph (c), the worker is assessed by
-- the Authority or self-insurer as having no current work capacity and likely to continue indefinitely to have no current
-- work capacity; or (b) the worker is a pre-12 November 1997 claimant who has a serious injury; or (c) in the case of a
-- worker whose second entitlement period expires on or after 31 March 2024, the Authority or self-insurer determines in
-- accordance with Subdivision 1A of Division 2 of Part 5 of the [2013 Act] that the worker -- (i) has no current work
-- capacity and is likely to continue indefinitely to have no current work capacity; and (ii) has a whole person impairment
-- of more than 20 per cent."
-- READING (fork F2): "subject to paragraph (c)" means that where (c) applies (a second entitlement period expiring on or
-- after 31 March 2024), (a) alone is not enough.
-- s 91E: serious injury, for a claim made before 12 November 1997, is "an injury ... in respect of which the worker's
-- degree of impairment, if assessed ... in accordance with section 91, would be 30 per cent or more".
-- "ceases ... unless" is the text's own no: JUST FALSE when no paragraph holds and s 93CD is not approved.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim`
      `the day my second entitlement period expires` IS A DATE
      `my degree of impairment under s 91 is 30 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am assessed as having no current work capacity indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am determined to have no current work capacity indefinitely and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my application under s 93CD has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`my weekly payments continue after the second entitlement period, for` `the claim` `expiring` `the day my second entitlement period expires` `serious` `my degree of impairment under s 91 is 30 per cent or more` `assessed` `I am assessed as having no current work capacity indefinitely` `determined` `I am determined to have no current work capacity indefinitely and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment` `s 93CD` `my application under s 93CD has been approved` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a)` OR `paragraph (b)` OR `paragraph (c)` OR `my application under s 93CD has been approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `paragraph (c) governs` MEANS `the day my second entitlement period expires` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 31 3 2024)
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
                (NOT `paragraph (c) governs`)
            AND `I am assessed as having no current work capacity indefinitely`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`
            WHEN `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` THEN `my degree of impairment under s 91 is 30 per cent or more`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
                `paragraph (c) governs`
            AND `I am determined to have no current work capacity indefinitely and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment`

@export Do my weekly payments go on after my second entitlement period ends (s 93C(1), s 93CD)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim` @desc Your kind of claim: a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant, one first made from 12 November 1997 to before 5 April 2010, or one first made on or after 5 April 2010
      `the day my second entitlement period expires` IS A DATE @desc The day your second entitlement period expires (or expired)
      `my degree of impairment under s 91 is 30 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a pre-12 November 1997 claim only: whether your degree of impairment, assessed under s 91, is 30% or more (a serious injury)
      `I am assessed as having no current work capacity indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer has assessed you as having no current work capacity and likely to continue indefinitely to have none
      `I am determined to have no current work capacity indefinitely and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer has determined, under the 2013 Act's Part 5 Division 2 Subdivision 1A, that you have no current work capacity indefinitely and a whole person impairment of more than 20%
      `my application under s 93CD has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application under s 93CD (to keep weekly payments while working at least 15 hours a week) has been approved
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` MEANS
    `my weekly payments continue after the second entitlement period, for` `the claim` `expiring` `the day my second entitlement period expires` `serious` `my degree of impairment under s 91 is 30 per cent or more` `assessed` `I am assessed as having no current work capacity indefinitely` `determined` `I am determined to have no current work capacity indefinitely and more than 20 per cent whole person impairment` `s 93CD` `my application under s 93CD has been approved`

§§ `ss 93A, 93B, 93C(2), 93CD(5) -- how much my weekly payment is`

DECLARE `My week` HAS
    `my pre-injury average weekly earnings`  IS A NUMBER  -- s 5A, as last varied under s 100
    `my current weekly earnings`             IS A NUMBER  -- 0 if none
    `I have a current work capacity`         IS A BOOLEAN -- a 2013 Act term (s 5(2)(a))
    `the deductible amount`                  IS A NUMBER  -- s 91E: employer's non-pecuniary benefits for the week
    `I have a serious injury`                IS A BOOLEAN -- s 91E, pre-12 November 1997 claims only

-- The rate "whichever is the lesser" of the two differences, read as never less than nothing (fork F4: the Act does not say
-- what a negative difference means; no payment is the reading taken).
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a `and` b `but not below nothing` MEANS max 0 (min a b)

-- The no-capacity line of ss 93A and 93B: "if the worker has no current work capacity and no current weekly earnings";
-- the other line: "if the worker has a current work capacity or has no current work capacity but has current weekly
-- earnings".
GIVEN `the week` IS A `My week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the week` `is on the no-capacity line` IF
        (NOT `the week`'s `I have a current work capacity`)
    AND `the week`'s `my current weekly earnings` EQUALS 0

-- s 93A(1), (2): "(a) ... 95 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings; or (ii) $1210 [$1510] --
-- whichever is the lesser; (b) ... the difference between 95 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings and
-- the worker's current weekly earnings; or (ii) the difference between $1210 [$1510] and the worker's current weekly
-- earnings -- whichever is the lesser."
-- s 93A(3): "(a) ... 95 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings, less the deductible amount; or (ii)
-- twice the State average weekly earnings ... (b) ... the difference between 95 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average
-- weekly earnings, less the deductible amount and the worker's current weekly earnings; or (ii) the difference between twice
-- the State average weekly earnings and the worker's current weekly earnings".
-- s 93B(1): "(a) if the worker has a serious injury, ... the difference between 90 per cent of the worker's pre-injury
-- average weekly earnings and 90 per cent of the worker's current weekly earnings; or (ii) the difference between $1210 and
-- 90 per cent of the worker's current weekly earnings ...; (b) if the worker does not have a serious injury but has no
-- current work capacity and has no current weekly earnings, ... 80 per cent ... or $1210 ...; (c) ... the difference between
-- 80 per cent ... and 80 per cent of the worker's current weekly earnings; or ... $1210 and 80 per cent ...".
-- s 93B(2), (3): as s 93A(2), (3), at 80 per cent, with 80 per cent of current weekly earnings.
-- s 93C(2): "(a) [pre-12 November 1997 claimant with a serious injury] the difference between 90 per cent ... and 90 per
-- cent of ... current weekly earnings; or ... $1210 and 90 per cent ...; (b) [pre-12 November 1997 claimant without] ... 80
-- per cent ... and, if the worker has current weekly earnings, 80 percent of those ...; (c) [12 November 1997 to 5 April
-- 2010] ... $1510 ...; (d) [on or after 5 April 2010] ... 80 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings,
-- less the deductible amount and, if the worker has current weekly earnings, 80 per cent of those earnings; or ... twice
-- the State average weekly earnings and ... 80 per cent ...".
-- s 93CD(5): "(a) [pre-12 November 1997 claimant] ... 80 per cent ... and 80 per cent ...; or ... $1210 and 80 per cent ...;
-- (b) [12 November 1997 to 5 April 2010] ... $1510 ...; (c) [on or after 5 April 2010] ... 80 per cent ..., less the
-- deductible amount and 80 per cent ...; or ... twice the State average weekly earnings and 80 per cent ...".
DECLARE `Weekly rate line` HAS
    `share of earnings`    IS A NUMBER  -- 95%, 90% or 80% of pre-injury average weekly earnings
    `share of current`     IS A NUMBER  -- the share of current weekly earnings taken off
    `less the deductible`  IS A BOOLEAN -- claims on or after 5 April 2010

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim`
      `the period` IS AN `Entitlement period`
      `the week` IS A `My week`
GIVETH A `Weekly rate line`
`the rate line for` `the claim` `in` `the period` `for` `the week` MEANS
    `Weekly rate line` WITH
        `share of earnings`   IS `earnings share`
        `share of current`    IS `current share`
        `less the deductible` IS `deductible applies`
    WHERE
        `pre-1997 serious` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`
            WHEN `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` THEN `the week`'s `I have a serious injury`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `deductible applies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`
            WHEN `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `earnings share` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the period`
            WHEN `the first entitlement period` THEN 0.95
            OTHERWISE
                IF `pre-1997 serious` THEN 0.9 ELSE 0.8
        `current share` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the period`
            WHEN `the first entitlement period` THEN 1
            OTHERWISE
                IF `pre-1997 serious` THEN 0.9 ELSE 0.8

-- The weekly payment on a line, given the ceiling. On the no-capacity line (s 93A(a), s 93B(1)(b), (2)(a), (3)(a)) there
-- are no current weekly earnings, so the two formulas agree with the other line's at nil earnings.
GIVEN `the line` IS A `Weekly rate line`
      `the week` IS A `My week`
      `the ceiling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly payment on` `the line` `for` `the week` `under the ceiling` `the ceiling` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the earnings part` MINUS `the current part`) `and` (`the ceiling` MINUS `the current part`) `but not below nothing`
    WHERE
        `the earnings part` MEANS
            IF `the line`'s `less the deductible`
            THEN (`the line`'s `share of earnings` TIMES `the week`'s `my pre-injury average weekly earnings`) MINUS `the week`'s `the deductible amount`
            ELSE `the line`'s `share of earnings` TIMES `the week`'s `my pre-injury average weekly earnings`
        `the current part` MEANS `the line`'s `share of current` TIMES `the week`'s `my current weekly earnings`

-- After the second entitlement period: s 93C(2) if s 93C(1)(a), (b) or (c) applies; s 93CD(5) if an application under
-- s 93CD(1) is approved and s 93C(1) does not apply; otherwise the entitlement has ceased (s 93C(1)): no weekly payment.
-- READING (fork F5): s 93C(2) is "a worker to whom subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) applies"; a worker continuing only
-- through s 93CD is paid at the s 93CD(5) rate, which for a pre-12 November 1997 claimant with a serious injury is 80%,
-- not the 90% of s 93C(2)(a).
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim`
      `the period` IS AN `Entitlement period`
      `the week` IS A `My week`
      `s 93C(1) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my application under s 93CD has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my weekly payment for` `the claim` `in` `the period` `for` `the week` `s 93C(1)` `s 93C(1) applies to me` `s 93CD` `my application under s 93CD has been approved` `in the week of` `the day of the week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the weekly payment ceiling for` `the claim` `in the week of` `the day of the week`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the ceiling for that year is not deposited)
    WHEN JUST `the ceiling` THEN
        CONSIDER `the period`
        WHEN `after the second entitlement period` THEN
            IF `s 93C(1) applies to me`
            THEN JUST (`the weekly payment on` (`the rate line for` `the claim` `in` `the period` `for` `the week`) `for` `the week` `under the ceiling` `the ceiling`)
            ELSE IF `my application under s 93CD has been approved`
                 THEN JUST (`the weekly payment on` (`the rate line for` `the claim` `in` `the period` `for` (`the week without a serious injury`)) `for` `the week` `under the ceiling` `the ceiling`)
                 ELSE JUST 0
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the weekly payment on` (`the rate line for` `the claim` `in` `the period` `for` `the week`) `for` `the week` `under the ceiling` `the ceiling`)
    WHERE
        `the week without a serious injury` MEANS `My week` WITH
            `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS `the week`'s `my pre-injury average weekly earnings`
            `my current weekly earnings`            IS `the week`'s `my current weekly earnings`
            `I have a current work capacity`        IS `the week`'s `I have a current work capacity`
            `the deductible amount`                 IS `the week`'s `the deductible amount`
            `I have a serious injury`               IS FALSE

@export How much is my weekly payment this week under the Accident Compensation Act 1985 (ss 93A, 93B, 93C(2), 93CD(5))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Weekly payments claim` @desc Your kind of claim: a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant, one first made from 12 November 1997 to before 5 April 2010, or one first made on or after 5 April 2010
      `the period` IS AN `Entitlement period` @desc Which entitlement period this week falls in (first, second, or after the second)
      `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-injury average weekly earnings in dollars a week, as last indexed under s 100
      `my current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are earning this week in dollars (0 if nothing)
      `I have a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can work in suitable employment though not in your pre-injury job (a current work capacity)
      `the deductible amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly value of non-pecuniary benefits (such as a car) your employer still provides you, in dollars (claims from 5 April 2010 only; 0 if none)
      `I have a serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a pre-12 November 1997 claim only: whether your degree of impairment under s 91 is 30% or more
      `s 93C(1) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the second entitlement period only: whether your weekly payments continue under s 93C(1) (no capacity indefinitely, a pre-1997 serious injury, or a determination of more than 20% impairment)
      `my application under s 93CD has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the second entitlement period only: whether your s 93CD application has been approved
      `the day of the week` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week the payment is for (the ceiling is known for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my weekly payment this week` MEANS
    `my weekly payment for` `the claim` `in` `the period` `for` (`My week` WITH
            `my pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS `my pre-injury average weekly earnings`
            `my current weekly earnings`            IS `my current weekly earnings`
            `I have a current work capacity`        IS `I have a current work capacity`
            `the deductible amount`                 IS `the deductible amount`
            `I have a serious injury`               IS `I have a serious injury`)
        `s 93C(1)` `s 93C(1) applies to me` `s 93CD` `my application under s 93CD has been approved` `in the week of` `the day of the week`

§§ `s 93CD -- keeping weekly payments while working at least 15 hours a week`

-- s 93CD(4): "The Authority or self-insurer must not approve an application under subsection (1) unless it is satisfied
-- that -- (a) the worker has returned to work (whether in self-employment or other employment) for a period of not less than
-- 15 hours per week and is in receipt of current weekly earnings, or current weekly earnings together with non-pecuniary
-- benefits within the meaning of section 5AB(1)(d), of at least $177 per week; and (b) because of the injury, the worker is,
-- and is likely to continue indefinitely to be, incapable of undertaking further additional employment or work which would
-- increase the worker's current weekly earnings; and (c) in the case of a worker whose second entitlement period expires on
-- or after 31 March 2024, the worker has a whole person impairment of more than 20 per cent."
-- s 313(1): s 93CD, except (5), as substituted in 2010 "applies in respect of an injury occurring on or after the
-- commencement date"; for an earlier injury the earlier text applies, which is not in the deposit. The commencement date
-- is not stated in the deposit; 5 April 2010, the date s 93A(3) uses, is taken (fork F6).
-- "must not approve ... unless" is the text's own no: JUST FALSE when a condition fails; JUST TRUE means it may be approved.
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the hours I work a week` IS A NUMBER
      `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `I am indefinitely incapable of more work that would raise my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my second entitlement period expires` IS A DATE
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`my s 93CD application can be approved, for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `decided on` `the day of the decision` `working` `the hours I work a week` `earning` `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` `incapable` `I am indefinitely incapable of more work that would raise my earnings` `expiring` `the day my second entitlement period expires` `impairment` `my whole person impairment` MEANS
    IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 5 4 2010)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: s 313(1)(b) keeps the earlier s 93CD, not in the deposit)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the s 93CD(4)(a) minimum weekly earnings on` `the day of the decision`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the indexed $177 for that year is not deposited)
         WHEN JUST `the minimum` THEN
             IF `(a) hours` AND (`my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` AT LEAST `the minimum`) AND `I am indefinitely incapable of more work that would raise my earnings` AND `(c) holds`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `(a) hours` MEANS `the hours I work a week` AT LEAST 15
        `(c) holds` MEANS (`the day my second entitlement period expires` `is before` (`the calendar date` 31 3 2024)) OR (`my whole person impairment` GREATER THAN 20)

@export Can my application to keep weekly payments while working be approved (s 93CD(4))?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer decides your application (the earnings minimum is known for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027)
      `the hours I work a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week you have returned to work, in a job or self-employment
      `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earn a week in dollars, with the value of any non-pecuniary benefits
      `I am indefinitely incapable of more work that would raise my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe or the self-insurer is satisfied that, because of the injury, you cannot (and likely never will be able to) take on more work that would raise your earnings
      `the day my second entitlement period expires` IS A DATE @desc The day your second entitlement period expires (or expired)
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment in per cent (it matters only if your second entitlement period expires on or after 31 March 2024)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my s 93CD application be approved` MEANS
    `my s 93CD application can be approved, for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `decided on` `the day of the decision` `working` `the hours I work a week` `earning` `my current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` `incapable` `I am indefinitely incapable of more work that would raise my earnings` `expiring` `the day my second entitlement period expires` `impairment` `my whole person impairment`

-- s 93CD(3): "the Authority or self-insurer must, within 28 days after receiving the application -- (a) approve or reject
-- the application; and (b) advise the worker in writing of its determination".
@export By when must WorkSafe or the self-insurer decide my s 93CD application (s 93CD(3))?
GIVEN `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe or the self-insurer received your s 93CD application
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my s 93CD application be decided` MEANS `the date` 28 `plain days after` `the day my application was received`

§§ `ss 93E, 93F -- whether my age stops my weekly payments`

-- s 93E: "If a worker is injured within the period of 130 weeks before attaining retirement age or after attaining
-- retirement age, the worker is entitled to weekly payments under this Part for not more than the first 130 weeks (whether
-- consecutive or not) of incapacity for work."
-- s 93F: "Subject to sections 93E and 93EA, a worker is not entitled to weekly payments under this Part after attaining
-- retirement age."
-- "retirement age" is a 2013 Act term (s 5(2)(a)): the day it is reached is asked. s 93EA (incapacity after retirement age
-- from hospital treatment) is not encoded: such a case answers NOTHING-kind only where the worker says it applies.
-- JUST TRUE: the age rules stop the payment this week. JUST FALSE: they do not (other rules may).
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day I reach retirement age` IS A DATE
      `the day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the weeks of incapacity paid so far, counting this week` IS A NUMBER
      `s 93EA applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the age rules stop my weekly payment, injured on` `the day of the injury` `retiring on` `the day I reach retirement age` `in the week of` `the day of the week` `weeks` `the weeks of incapacity paid so far, counting this week` `s 93EA` `s 93EA applies to me` MEANS
    IF `s 93EA applies to me`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent here: s 93EA is not encoded)
    ELSE IF `s 93E applies`
         THEN JUST (`the weeks of incapacity paid so far, counting this week` GREATER THAN 130)
         ELSE JUST (`the day of the week` `is on or after` `the day I reach retirement age`)
    WHERE
        `s 93E applies` MEANS `the day of the injury` `is on or after` (`the date` (0 MINUS 910) `plain days after` `the day I reach retirement age`)

@export Does my age stop my weekly payments this week (ss 93E, 93F: retirement age and the 130-week rule)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured
      `the day I reach retirement age` IS A DATE @desc The day you reach retirement age (your age pension age, as the 2013 Act defines retirement age)
      `the day of the week` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week you are asking about
      `the weeks of incapacity paid so far, counting this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting this week, how many weeks of incapacity for work you have been paid weekly payments for, consecutive or not
      `s 93EA applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are claiming under s 93EA (incapacity after retirement age caused by hospital treatment for the injury)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my age stop my weekly payments` MEANS
    `the age rules stop my weekly payment, injured on` `the day of the injury` `retiring on` `the day I reach retirement age` `in the week of` `the day of the week` `weeks` `the weeks of incapacity paid so far, counting this week` `s 93EA` `s 93EA applies to me`

§§ `s 93CE -- superannuation contributions`

-- s 93CE(1): if "(b) compensation in the form of weekly payments -- (i) has been paid or is payable to the worker in respect
-- of that injury for an aggregate period of 52 weeks (whether or not consecutive); and (ii) has not ceased to be paid or
-- payable in respect of that injury; and (c) the worker has not attained retirement age -- the Authority or self-insurer
-- must, subject to the worker nominating a complying fund ... and providing details of his or her tax file number to the
-- trustee of the nominated complying fund within 3 months of receipt of a notice under subsection (4), pay ...
-- compensation in the form of superannuation contributions". (2): not for a period in which the employer makes
-- contributions above the superannuation guarantee to discharge an injury obligation. (3): "the charge percentage of the
-- compensation in the form of weekly payments payable ... after the expiry of the period referred to in subsection
-- (1)(b)(i)". (8): "charge percentage means the percentage applicable for the time being under section 19(2) of the
-- Superannuation Act" (the Commonwealth Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992): asked.
-- s 315: s 93CE "applies in respect of injuries occurring on or after the commencement date" (5 April 2010 taken, fork F6).
-- The weekly contribution owed, JUST 0 where the section gives none, NOTHING for an earlier injury.
-- READING (fork F7): the 3-month nomination condition limits what is owed before the details are given (s 93CE(4)(g));
-- it is asked as "I have nominated a fund and given my tax file number".
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the weeks of weekly payments so far` IS A NUMBER
      `my weekly payments have ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer pays extra contributions for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have nominated a fund and given my tax file number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my weekly payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the charge percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the superannuation contribution for my week, injured on` `the day of the injury` `after` `the weeks of weekly payments so far` `ceased` `my weekly payments have ceased` `retired` `I have reached retirement age` `employer extra` `my employer pays extra contributions for this injury` `nominated` `I have nominated a fund and given my tax file number` `on a payment of` `my weekly payment` `at` `the charge percentage` MEANS
    IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 5 4 2010)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 315 confines s 93CE to later injuries)
    ELSE IF `owed`
         THEN JUST (`my weekly payment` TIMES `the charge percentage` DIVIDED BY 100)
         ELSE JUST 0
    WHERE
        `owed` MEANS
                `the weeks of weekly payments so far` GREATER THAN 52
            AND (NOT `my weekly payments have ceased`)
            AND (NOT `I have reached retirement age`)
            AND (NOT `my employer pays extra contributions for this injury`)
            AND `I have nominated a fund and given my tax file number`

@export How much superannuation must be paid for me this week on top of my weekly payments (s 93CE)?
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured
      `the weeks of weekly payments so far` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting this week, how many weeks weekly payments have been paid or are payable to you for this injury (contributions start after 52)
      `my weekly payments have ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your weekly payments have stopped
      `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached retirement age
      `my employer pays extra contributions for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is paying superannuation above the guarantee amount to meet an obligation that arises because of your injury
      `I have nominated a fund and given my tax file number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have nominated a complying super fund to WorkSafe or the self-insurer and given the fund your tax file number
      `my weekly payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment this week, in dollars
      `the charge percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The superannuation guarantee charge percentage now in force, in per cent (for example 12)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` MEANS
    `the superannuation contribution for my week, injured on` `the day of the injury` `after` `the weeks of weekly payments so far` `ceased` `my weekly payments have ceased` `retired` `I have reached retirement age` `employer extra` `my employer pays extra contributions for this injury` `nominated` `I have nominated a fund and given my tax file number` `on a payment of` `my weekly payment` `at` `the charge percentage`

§ `Compensation for non-economic loss (s 98C)`

§§ `s 98C(2A) and Schedule 2 -- my impairment benefit rating`

-- Schedule 2, column 1 "Whole person impairment as assessed in accordance with Chapter 3 of the A.M.A. Guides", column 2
-- "Modified whole person impairment": 5 10.00, 6 10.20, 7 10.40, 8 10.60, 9 10.80, 10 11.00, 11 11.95, 12 12.90, 13 13.85,
-- 14 14.80, 15 15.75, 16 16.70, 17 17.65, 18 18.60, 19 19.55, 20 20.50, 21 21.45, 22 22.40, 23 23.35, 24 24.30, 25 25.25,
-- 26 26.20, 27 27.15, 28 28.10, 29 29.05. (From 5 to 10 the step is 0.20; from 10 to 29 it is 0.95.)
GIVEN `the Chapter 3 impairment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the Schedule 2 modified impairment for` `the Chapter 3 impairment` MEANS
    IF `the Chapter 3 impairment` AT LEAST 5 AND `the Chapter 3 impairment` AT MOST 29 AND `the Chapter 3 impairment` EQUALS FLOOR `the Chapter 3 impairment`
    THEN IF `the Chapter 3 impairment` AT MOST 10
         THEN JUST (10 PLUS ((`the Chapter 3 impairment` MINUS 5) TIMES 0.2))
         ELSE JUST (11 PLUS ((`the Chapter 3 impairment` MINUS 10) TIMES 0.95))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: Schedule 2 lists only whole numbers from 5 to 29)

DECLARE `Rating kind` IS ONE OF
    `a modified whole person impairment`   -- s 98C(2A)(a)(i)
    `a modified spinal impairment`         -- s 98C(2A)(a)(ii)
    `a spinal impairment`                  -- s 98C(2A)(a)(iii)
    `the degree of impairment`             -- s 98C(2A)(a)(iv), (b)

DECLARE `Rating` HAS
    `the rating`      IS A NUMBER
    `the rating kind` IS A `Rating kind`

§§ `s 98C(2) -- the amount for a rating (permanent impairment other than psychiatric)`

-- s 98C(2): "(a) if the worker's impairment benefit rating is less than 10% -- ... zero; (b) subject to section 265, if the
-- worker's impairment benefit rating -- (i) is a modified whole person impairment ... and is not less than 10% and less than
-- 11% -- ... $11 670 + [(D - 10) x $9940]; (ii) is a modified spinal impairment ... and is not less than 10% and less than 11%
-- -- ... {$11 670 + [(D - 10) x $9940]} x 1.1; (c) ... (i) is not less than 10% and not more than 30% and paragraph (b) does not
-- apply ... $18 810 + [(D - 10) x $2830]; (ii) is a spinal impairment (within the meaning of subsection (2A)(a)(ii) or (iii))
-- and is not less than 10% and less than 30% and paragraph (b) does not apply ... the lesser of {$18 810 + [(D - 10)
-- x $2830]} x 1.1 and $18 810 + [20 x $2830]; (d) ... more than 30% and not more than 70% ... $75 260 + [(D - 30) x $4700]; (e)
-- ... more than 70% and not more than 80% ... the lesser of $262 070 + [(D - 70) x $29 330] and $555 350; (f) ... more than 80%
-- ... $555 350 -- where D is the worker's impairment benefit rating expressed as a number."
-- s 265 / note to (2A): (2)(b) and (2A)(a)(i), (ii) "do not apply with respect to injuries that occurred before" 3
-- December 2003 (the date (3AA) and (3AB) use for the commencement of the 2003 amendment).
-- s 98C(3AA), (3AB): for an injury before 3 December 2003, the (2)(c) and (2)(d) amounts are those "applying at the time
-- of the injury"; for one on or after 3 December 2003 and before 1 July 2010, the (2)(b) and (2)(c) amounts are. Those
-- amounts are not in the deposit: NOTHING. The (2)(d) amounts for 3 December 2003 to 30 June 2010, and every amount for
-- 1 July 2010 to 30 June 2014, are the printed ones, read literally (NOTES.md finding 8).
-- Over 70% the relevant date is the date of the calculation (s 98C(1A)): the varied figures (aca-amounts).
-- A rating of exactly 30% that is a spinal impairment falls in (c)(i): (c)(ii) is "less than 30%".
GIVEN `the rating` IS A `Rating`
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 98C(2) amount for` `the rating` `for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF D LESS THAN 10 THEN JUST 0
           IF D LESS THAN 11 AND `(b) can apply` AND `is modified whole person` THEN `(b)(i) answer`
           IF D LESS THAN 11 AND `(b) can apply` AND `is modified spinal` THEN `(b)(ii) answer`
           IF D AT MOST 30 THEN `(c) answer`
           IF D AT MOST 70 THEN `(d) answer`
           OTHERWISE `(e) or (f) answer`
    WHERE
        D MEANS `the rating`'s `the rating`
        `(b) can apply` MEANS `the day of the injury` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 3 12 2003)
        `before 1 July 2010` MEANS `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2010)
        `is modified whole person` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the rating`'s `the rating kind`
            WHEN `a modified whole person impairment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is modified spinal` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the rating`'s `the rating kind`
            WHEN `a modified spinal impairment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is spinal for (c)(ii)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the rating`'s `the rating kind`
            WHEN `a modified spinal impairment` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a spinal impairment` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `(b)(i) amount` MEANS `s 98C(2)(b) base` PLUS ((D MINUS 10) TIMES `s 98C(2)(b) per point`)
        `(c)(i) amount` MEANS `s 98C(2)(c) base` PLUS ((D MINUS 10) TIMES `s 98C(2)(c) per point`)
        `(b)(i) answer` MEANS
            IF `before 1 July 2010`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: (3AB)(a) amount then in force)
            ELSE JUST `(b)(i) amount`
        `(b)(ii) answer` MEANS
            IF `before 1 July 2010`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: (3AB)(a) amount then in force)
            ELSE JUST (`(b)(i) amount` TIMES 1.1)
        `(c) answer` MEANS
            IF `before 1 July 2010`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: (3AA)(a) or (3AB)(b) amount then in force)
            ELSE IF `is spinal for (c)(ii)` AND D LESS THAN 30
                 THEN JUST (min (`(c)(i) amount` TIMES 1.1) (`s 98C(2)(c) base` PLUS (20 TIMES `s 98C(2)(c) per point`)))
                 ELSE JUST `(c)(i) amount`
        `(d) answer` MEANS
            IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 3 12 2003)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: (3AA)(b) amount then in force)
            ELSE JUST (`s 98C(2)(d) base` PLUS ((D MINUS 30) TIMES `s 98C(2)(d) per point`))
        `(e) or (f) answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the s 98C upper band figures on` `the day of the calculation`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: no deposited notice for that year)
            WHEN JUST `the figures` THEN
                IF D AT MOST 80
                THEN JUST (min (`the figures`'s `the base over 70` PLUS ((D MINUS 70) TIMES `the figures`'s `the amount per point`)) (`the figures`'s `the upper maximum`))
                ELSE JUST (`the figures`'s `the upper maximum`)

-- s 98C(2A): "a worker's impairment benefit rating is -- (a) if the worker's degree of impairment consists of, or includes,
-- a whole person impairment assessed in accordance with Chapter 3 of the A.M.A. Guides and that whole person impairment is
-- not less than 5% and not more than 29% -- (i) subject to section 265, the modified whole person impairment set out in
-- column 2 of Schedule 2 opposite the relevant whole person impairment as assessed in accordance with Chapter 3; (ii)
-- subject to section 265, the modified whole person impairment set out in column 2 of Schedule 2 opposite the relevant
-- whole person impairment as assessed in accordance with Chapter 3 for a spinal impairment; (iii) if subparagraph (ii) does
-- not apply, the worker's degree of impairment as assessed in accordance with Chapter 3 for a spinal impairment; (iv) the
-- worker's degree of impairment -- whichever provides the worker with the higher amount for non-economic loss under
-- subsection (2); (b) in any other case, the worker's degree of impairment."
-- READING (fork F8): (i) is the Schedule 2 figure for a Chapter 3 impairment that is not a spinal impairment, (ii) for one
-- that is; (iii) applies when (ii) does not (an injury before 3 December 2003, s 265). Every candidate open on the facts is
-- priced under (2) and the highest amount wins.
GIVEN `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `my Chapter 3 impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my s 98C(2) amount for a degree of` `my degree of impairment` `with Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    IF `my Chapter 3 impairment` AT LEAST 5 AND `my Chapter 3 impairment` AT MOST 29
    THEN `the highest of` (`price` (`Rating` WITH `the rating` IS `my degree of impairment`, `the rating kind` IS `the degree of impairment`)) `and` `the other candidate`
    ELSE `price` (`Rating` WITH `the rating` IS `my degree of impairment`, `the rating kind` IS `the degree of impairment`)
    WHERE
        GIVEN r IS A `Rating`
        GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
        `price` r MEANS `the s 98C(2) amount for` r `for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation`
        `s 265 shuts out the modified figures` MEANS `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 3 12 2003)
        `the other candidate` MEANS
            IF `s 265 shuts out the modified figures`
            THEN IF `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment`
                 THEN `price` (`Rating` WITH `the rating` IS `my Chapter 3 impairment`, `the rating kind` IS `a spinal impairment`)
                 ELSE NOTHING -- not a candidate: (i) is shut out by s 265 and (iii) is for a spinal impairment
            ELSE CONSIDER `the Schedule 2 modified impairment for` `my Chapter 3 impairment`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- not a candidate: no Schedule 2 row (a fraction of a per cent)
                 WHEN JUST `the modified` THEN
                     IF `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment`
                     THEN `price` (`Rating` WITH `the rating` IS `the modified`, `the rating kind` IS `a modified spinal impairment`)
                     ELSE `price` (`Rating` WITH `the rating` IS `the modified`, `the rating kind` IS `a modified whole person impairment`)

-- The higher of two amounts, where either may be unknown: unknown if the degree's own amount is unknown, or if the other
-- candidate is unknown for want of a deposited figure.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE NUMBER, b IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the highest of` a `and` b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (max x y)

§§ `s 98C(3) -- psychiatric impairment`

-- s 98C(3): "(a) if the worker's degree of impairment is less than 30% -- ... zero; (b) if ... 30% -- ... subject to
-- subsection (3AA), ... $18 810 + [(D - 10) x $2830]; (c) ... more than 30% and not more than 70% -- ... subject to subsection
-- (3AA), ... $75 260 + [(D - 30) x $4700]; (d) ... more than 70% and not more than 80% -- ... the lesser of $262 070 + [(D -
-- 70) x $29 330] and $555 350; (e) ... more than 80% -- ... $555 350".
-- (3AA)(c), (d) and (3AB)(c), (d): for an injury before 1 July 2010 the (3)(b), (c) amounts are those then in force: NOTHING.
GIVEN D IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 98C(3) amount for a psychiatric impairment of` D `for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF D LESS THAN 30 THEN JUST 0
           IF D AT MOST 70 THEN `(b) or (c) answer`
           OTHERWISE `(d) or (e) answer`
    WHERE
        `(b) or (c) answer` MEANS
            IF `the day of the injury` `is before` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2010)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: (3AA) or (3AB) amount then in force)
            ELSE IF D EQUALS 30
                 THEN JUST (`s 98C(2)(c) base` PLUS ((D MINUS 10) TIMES `s 98C(2)(c) per point`))
                 ELSE JUST (`s 98C(2)(d) base` PLUS ((D MINUS 30) TIMES `s 98C(2)(d) per point`))
        `(d) or (e) answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the s 98C upper band figures on` `the day of the calculation`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: no deposited notice for that year)
            WHEN JUST `the figures` THEN
                IF D AT MOST 80
                THEN JUST (min (`the figures`'s `the base over 70` PLUS ((D MINUS 70) TIMES `the figures`'s `the amount per point`)) (`the figures`'s `the upper maximum`))
                ELSE JUST (`the figures`'s `the upper maximum`)

§§ `My lump sum for non-economic loss`

DECLARE `Kind of non-economic loss` IS ONE OF
    `permanent impairment other than psychiatric`
    `permanent psychiatric impairment`
    `the loss of a foetus`

-- s 98C(4): "The amount of the non-economic loss in respect of an injury resulting in the loss of a foetus or of the loss of
-- more than one foetus is $67 660." s 98D: paid as a lump sum.
-- The amount the section's formulas give, before the s 98C(11) maximum.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of non-economic loss`
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `my Chapter 3 impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 98C formula amount for` `the kind` `degree` `my degree of impairment` `Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    IF `the day of the injury` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2014)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 4(1)(a), the Act applies to injuries before 1 July 2014)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `the loss of a foetus` THEN JUST `s 98C(4) amount for loss of a foetus`
         WHEN `permanent psychiatric impairment` THEN `the s 98C(3) amount for a psychiatric impairment of` `my degree of impairment` `for an injury on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation`
         WHEN `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` THEN `my s 98C(2) amount for a degree of` `my degree of impairment` `with Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation`

@export What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss, before the s 98C(11) maximum?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of non-economic loss` @desc What the lump sum is for: permanent impairment other than psychiatric, permanent psychiatric impairment, or the loss of a foetus
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of impairment in per cent, as assessed under s 91
      `my Chapter 3 impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Any whole person impairment assessed under Chapter 3 of the AMA Guides (the spine and musculoskeletal chapter) that your degree of impairment includes, in per cent (0 if none)
      `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment (assessed solely under section 3.3 of Chapter 3)
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured (before 1 July 2014)
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is calculated (it matters if your rating is over 70%; figures are known for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` MEANS
    `the s 98C formula amount for` `the kind` `degree` `my degree of impairment` `Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation`

-- s 98C(11): "Despite anything to the contrary in this section or section 98E, a worker is not entitled to an amount of
-- compensation for non-economic loss under this section or section 98E or both that exceeds the maximum amount payable
-- under this section as in force at the date of the relevant injury." (NOTES.md finding 9.)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of non-economic loss`
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `my Chapter 3 impairment` IS A NUMBER
      `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my s 98C lump sum for` `the kind` `degree` `my degree of impairment` `Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 98C formula amount for` `the kind` `degree` `my degree of impairment` `Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the amount` THEN
        IF `my degree of impairment` AT MOST 70
        THEN JUST `the amount` -- the (2)(a)-(d), (3)(a)-(c) and (4) amounts stay below the s 98C maximum (fork F3)
        ELSE CONSIDER `the s 98C(11) maximum for an injury on` `the day of the injury`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the maximum in force at the injury date)
             WHEN JUST `the maximum` THEN JUST (min `the amount` `the maximum`)

@export How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss under s 98C (with the s 98C(11) maximum at the date of my injury)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of non-economic loss` @desc What the lump sum is for: permanent impairment other than psychiatric, permanent psychiatric impairment, or the loss of a foetus
      `my degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of impairment in per cent, as assessed under s 91
      `my Chapter 3 impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Any whole person impairment assessed under Chapter 3 of the AMA Guides that your degree of impairment includes, in per cent (0 if none)
      `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you were injured (before 1 July 2014)
      `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE @desc The day the amount is calculated (figures over 70% are known for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` MEANS
    `my s 98C lump sum for` `the kind` `degree` `my degree of impairment` `Chapter 3` `my Chapter 3 impairment` `spinal` `my Chapter 3 impairment is a spinal impairment` `injured on` `the day of the injury` `calculated on` `the day of the calculation`
